═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§1  ORGANISM GENERATOR PIPELINE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The Organism Generator is the deployment pipeline that transforms source
  organism architecture into deployable substrate-specific packages.

  Pipeline Stages:

  ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────┐    ┌──────────┐
  │ TEMPLATE │───▶│  SEED    │───▶│ CANISTER │───▶│SUBSTRATE │
  └──────────┘    └──────────┘    └──────────┘    └──────────┘
       │               │               │               │
   Architecture    Minimal viable   Deployable      Running on
   blueprint       organism         container       target
   from source     compiled         forged          substrate

  STAGE 1 — TEMPLATE
    The Organism Generator reads the full architecture from source —
    all 20 packages, all 8 terminals, all 18 AI systems, all governance
    rules. It produces an architecture template: a declarative blueprint
    of what the organism needs on the target substrate.

    Template Contents:
      template.terminals ......... Which terminals to deploy
      template.ais ............... Which AI systems to include
      template.packages ......... Which packages to bundle
      template.governance ....... Governance configuration
      template.security ......... Security posture settings
      template.substrate ........ Target substrate parameters

  STAGE 2 — SEED
    The Seed Compiler takes the template and compiles it into a minimal
    viable organism (MVO) — the smallest possible deployment that can
    bootstrap into a full organism on the target substrate.

    Seed Contents:
      seed.kernel ............... organism-kernel (always included)
      seed.security ............. nova-encryption + SAEIS bootstrap
      seed.governance ........... governance-core (minimal voting)
      seed.memory ............... memory-palace (single tier)
      seed.bus .................. sovereign-bus (event routing)
      seed.bootstrap ............ Self-expansion protocol

    The seed is intentionally minimal. Once deployed, it bootstraps
    by pulling remaining packages through the Spinal Cord Bus.

  STAGE 3 — CANISTER
    The Canister Forge takes the seed and compacts it into a deployable
    canister — a sealed, self-contained unit optimized for the target
    substrate. Canisters are the deployment unit of the organism.

    Canister Properties:
      canister.format ........... Substrate-specific binary format
      canister.signature ........ Ed25519 signed by FABRICATOR AGI
      canister.encryption ....... Nova-encrypted payload
      canister.manifest ......... Deployment manifest with checksums
      canister.rollback ......... Previous version for rollback

  STAGE 4 — SUBSTRATE
    The canister is deployed to the target substrate. FABRICATOR AGI
    manages the deployment, monitors the bootstrap sequence, and verifies
    that the organism is fully operational on the new substrate.


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§2  FIVE DEPLOYMENT SUBSTRATES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The organism deploys across 5 substrates. Each substrate provides
  different capabilities, and the organism adapts its deployment
  profile to leverage each substrate's strengths.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  SUBSTRATE 1 — ICP BLOCKCHAIN

  The Internet Computer Protocol. On-chain deployment as Motoko canisters.
  Provides: immutability, decentralized execution, permanent storage.

  Canister: icp/medina/Medina.mo → compiled Motoko → ICP canister
  Runtime:  Motoko VM on ICP replicas
  Storage:  Stable memory (persistent across upgrades)
  Identity: Internet Identity + sovereign key binding

  Status: [■■■■■■■■■■] DEPLOYED — Medina.mo canister live on ICP

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  SUBSTRATE 2 — WEB

  Browser-native deployment as web workers and service workers.
  Provides: universal access, offline capability, client-side sovereignty.

  Canister: WASM bundle + service worker → browser runtime
  Runtime:  ANIMA Runtime (Anima Computandi Machina) in browser
  Storage:  IndexedDB + encrypted local storage
  Identity: Device-bound keys + sovereign session tokens

  Status: [■■■■■■■■■■] DEPLOYED — Web deployment active

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  SUBSTRATE 3 — DEEP QUANTUM

  Quantum circuit deployment for quantum-advantage computations.
  Provides: quantum parallelism, superposition-based search, entanglement.

  Canister: Quantum circuit definition → quantum processor
  Runtime:  Quantum circuit executor
  Storage:  Classical memory with quantum state snapshots
  Identity: Quantum key distribution (QKD) bound identities

  Status: [■■■■░░░░░░] RESEARCH — Quantum deployment in development

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  SUBSTRATE 4 — ENCRYPTION MODEL

  Fully homomorphic encryption (FHE) deployment. Computation on encrypted
  data without decryption.
  Provides: compute-on-encrypted, zero-knowledge proofs, privacy.

  Canister: FHE-compiled organism → encrypted compute node
  Runtime:  FHE evaluation engine
  Storage:  Encrypted-at-rest, encrypted-in-compute
  Identity: Zero-knowledge identity proofs

  Status: [■■■■■░░░░░] PROTOTYPE — FHE deployment in prototype

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  SUBSTRATE 5 — HYBRID

  Multi-substrate deployment spanning two or more substrates simultaneously.
  Provides: substrate redundancy, cross-substrate coordination, resilience.

  Canister: Meta-canister containing sub-canisters for each substrate
  Runtime:  Cross-substrate orchestration layer
  Storage:  Distributed across participating substrates
  Identity: Federated identity across substrates

  Status: [■■■■■■■░░░] DEVELOPMENT — Hybrid deployment in development


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§3  CANISTER FORGE — COMPACT SDK DEPLOYMENT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The Canister Forge is the compilation engine that compacts full SDKs
  into deployable canisters. It is operated by FABRICATOR AGI (TERMINAL 06).

  Forge Process:
    1. INPUT — Full SDK source (20 packages, dependencies, configs)
    2. ANALYZE — Dependency graph analysis, dead code elimination
    3. COMPACT — Tree-shaking, minification, compression
    4. SEAL — Nova encryption, Ed25519 signing, manifest generation
    5. OUTPUT — Sealed canister ready for substrate deployment

  Compaction Ratios:
    ICP Canister ......... ~85% reduction (Motoko-optimized)
    Web Canister ......... ~70% reduction (WASM + tree-shake)
    Quantum Canister ..... ~60% reduction (circuit optimization)
    FHE Canister ......... ~50% reduction (FHE overhead retained)
    Hybrid Canister ...... ~40% reduction (multi-substrate overhead)

  Forge Security:
    Every canister produced by the Forge is:
      • Signed by FABRICATOR AGI with Ed25519
      • Encrypted with Nova envelope encryption
      • Checksummed with SHA-512
      • Logged to the deployment ledger
      • Verified by VERIFICATOR before release


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§4  SEED COMPILER — MINIMAL VIABLE ORGANISM
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The Seed Compiler produces the smallest possible organism that can
  bootstrap into a full deployment. Seeds are self-expanding — once
  deployed, they pull remaining components through the Spinal Cord Bus.

  Seed Compilation Rules:
    ALWAYS INCLUDE:
      organism-kernel ........ The heart. Non-negotiable.
      nova-encryption ........ Security from first byte.
      sovereign-bus .......... Communication backbone.
      governance-core ........ Minimal governance for bootstrap decisions.

    CONDITIONALLY INCLUDE (based on substrate):
      memory-palace .......... If substrate supports persistent storage
      consensus-engine ....... If multi-agent deployment
      sandbox-layer .......... If substrate is multi-tenant

    EXCLUDE FROM SEED (pulled post-bootstrap):
      All other packages, all MACHINA engines, all AI models

  Bootstrap Sequence:
    1. Seed deployed to substrate
    2. organism-kernel initializes — heartbeat begins
    3. nova-encryption establishes secure channel to Spinal Cord Bus
    4. sovereign-bus connects to existing organism mesh
    5. governance-core activates — bootstrap governance operational
    6. Remaining packages pulled via Spinal Cord Bus
    7. AI systems initialized in terminal order (01 → 06 → α → β)
    8. Full organism operational — FABRICATOR reports success


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§5  SPINAL CORD BUS — SHARED MEMORY BACKBONE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The Spinal Cord Bus is the shared memory backbone that connects all
  substrates. Every deployed organism instance communicates through the
  Bus, regardless of substrate.

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │                      SPINAL CORD BUS                                │
  │                                                                     │
  │  ┌─────┐   ┌─────┐   ┌─────┐   ┌─────┐   ┌─────┐                │
  │  │ ICP │───│ Web │───│Quant│───│ FHE │───│Hybrd│                │
  │  └──┬──┘   └──┬──┘   └──┬──┘   └──┬──┘   └──┬──┘                │
  │     │         │         │         │         │                      │
  │  ┌──┴─────────┴─────────┴─────────┴─────────┴──┐                  │
  │  │         SHARED MEMORY LAYER                   │                  │
  │  │  Memory-palace sync │ Knowledge-graph sync     │                  │
  │  │  Team-vault sync    │ Temporal-memory sync     │                  │
  │  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘                  │
  │                                                                     │
  │  Protocol:    φ-timed heartbeat sync @ 618ms intervals             │
  │  Encryption:  Nova end-to-end encryption on all bus traffic         │
  │  Routing:     PRAEFECTUS (ALPHA α) optimized mesh routing          │
  │  Monitoring:  CUSTOS AGI (TERMINAL 05) continuous surveillance     │
  │                                                                     │
  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Bus Operations:
    SYNC ............. Synchronize memory state across substrates
    ROUTE ............ Route signals between substrate instances
    BRIDGE ........... Translate between substrate-native formats
    HEAL ............. Repair broken connections, resync divergent state
    SCALE ............ Add/remove substrate instances dynamically


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§6  DIGITAL TWIN DEPLOYMENT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Client businesses are deployed as digital twins within the organism.
  Each twin is a sandboxed organism instance with its own terminal
  subset, memory tier, and governance voice.

  Digital Twin Architecture:
    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │  CLIENT DIGITAL TWIN                                 │
    │                                                       │
    │  ┌─────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌────────────┐  │
    │  │ Twin Kernel  │  │ Twin Memory  │  │ Twin Gov   │  │
    │  │ (sandboxed)  │  │ (isolated)   │  │ (scoped)   │  │
    │  └──────┬───────┘  └──────┬───────┘  └─────┬──────┘  │
    │         └─────────────────┼─────────────────┘         │
    │                           │                            │
    │              Spinal Cord Bus (filtered)                │
    │                           │                            │
    └───────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┘
                                │
                    Main Organism Mesh

  Twin Deployment Steps:
    1. Client onboarded via /api/company endpoint
    2. FABRICATOR AGI generates twin template from client profile
    3. Seed Compiler produces twin-specific seed
    4. Canister Forge packages twin canister
    5. Twin deployed to client's preferred substrate
    6. Twin connects to main organism via filtered Spinal Cord Bus
    7. Twin governance voice registered in federated voting


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§7  20 MULTI-IDENTITY TECHNOLOGIES & DEPLOYMENT ROLES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The organism deploys 20 multi-identity technologies — each one an
  identity layer that the organism presents to different substrates,
  clients, and external systems.

  Identity Technologies:
    01. Sovereign Key Identity ......... Root organism identity (Ed25519)
    02. Internet Identity .............. ICP-native browser auth
    03. Device-Bound Identity .......... Hardware key binding
    04. Session Token Identity ......... Ephemeral session auth (SAT)
    05. Role-Based Identity ............ Agent role identity
    06. Team Identity .................. Team-vault group identity
    07. Cross-Substrate Identity ....... Federated multi-substrate ID
    08. Digital Twin Identity .......... Client twin identity
    09. Canister Identity .............. Per-canister unique identity
    10. Signal Identity ................ Per-signal source authentication
    11. Contract Identity .............. CPL contract signer identity
    12. Governance Identity ............ Voting bill participant identity
    13. Memory Identity ................ Per-memory-tier access identity
    14. Encryption Identity ............ Nova key pair identity
    15. API Identity ................... Intelligence Wire caller identity
    16. Registry Identity .............. Package registry publisher identity
    17. Substrate Identity ............. Per-substrate deployment identity
    18. Quantum Identity ............... QKD-based quantum substrate ID
    19. FHE Identity ................... Zero-knowledge proof identity
    20. Ecosystem Identity ............. External system federation ID

  Deployment Role per Identity:
    Each identity technology has a specific deployment role — it
    authenticates a specific class of deployment operation. FABRICATOR
    AGI selects the appropriate identity for each deployment action.


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§8  CROSS-SUBSTRATE CANISTER COMMUNICATION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Canisters on different substrates communicate through the Spinal Cord
  Bus using a substrate-agnostic message protocol.

  Message Format:
    message.source_substrate ...... Origin substrate identifier
    message.target_substrate ...... Destination substrate identifier
    message.source_canister ....... Origin canister identity
    message.target_canister ....... Destination canister identity
    message.payload ............... Nova-encrypted message body
    message.signature ............. Ed25519 signature from source
    message.timestamp ............. φ-timed message timestamp
    message.priority .............. P0-P4 priority level

  Translation Layer:
    When a message crosses substrate boundaries, the MOTUS ENGINE AI
    (ALPHA α) translates between substrate-native formats:
      ICP ↔ Web:     Candid ↔ JSON (medina-translate)
      ICP ↔ Quantum: Candid ↔ Circuit Definition
      Web ↔ FHE:     JSON ↔ FHE-encrypted payload
      Any ↔ Hybrid:  Native format ↔ meta-format


